            <h1> Setting the Record Straight on Hinduism/ 'Sanatana Dharma'</h1> 
            <h2>CELEBRATING 5092nd ANNIVERSARY OF THE DAY "ŚRĪMAD BHAGAVAD GĪTĀ" WAS FIRST SUNG</h2>
        <br>---------------------------------------------------
        <p style="text-align: center;"><i>नोट: <a href="#hindi">हिंदी संस्करण</a> भी नीचे उपलब्ध है। </i></p>

        <div class="auth-box-main"> 
        <h2 id="1summary">1.0 SUMMARY </h2>
        <p>-------------</p>
        <p style="text-align: left;">'Sanatana Dharma'/ Hinduism is the third largest faith in the world, and yet its image is that of a people of a distant land with thousands of Gods, and hence leading a corrupt life. This blog refutes such common misconceptions using bonafide sources, and shows the "real" faith's practice today by its adherents across the world. It uses the oath book - the Śrīmad Bhagavad Gītā to counter unjust image associated with us, the adherents of the oldest faith in the world still being practiced. Finally it points to sources, which outline the chronology of events that led to this awful image of our blessing (our faith), that we have to cope with today.</p>
        
		   <p><i id="mm1gitajayanti" style="text-align: center;"> Item 1: "ŚRĪMAD BHAGAVAD GĪTĀ" JĀYĀNTI CELEBRATIONS - 01 DECEMBER 2025, IN LOWER HUTT, NEW ZEALAND</i></p>	
        <p><img src="images/GitaJayanti2025.jpg" alt="Gita Jayanti in Lower Hutt" style="center-image;width:600px;"></p> 
 <h2 id="1background">2.0 BACKGROUND </h2>
<p style="text-align: left;"  class="indent">I am so upset that most people say Hinduism has no oath book, it is polytheistic/'does not have one god' and has an engrained degenerate caste system, where people belonging to some castes are even barred from entering their place of worship. It makes my blood curdle with great vengeance, that even Hindus repeat these lies and firmly believe it. I see it like a civil war.</p>

 <h2 id="3resolution">3.0 RESOLUTION </h2>

<p style="text-align: left;"  class="indent">But, since I am a non violent follower of Mahatma Gandhi ji, please find here just evidence of 'Sanatana Dharma' /Hinduism oath book - ŚRĪMAD BHAGAVAD GĪTĀ. It is a dialogue between an individual and God, Śrī Śrī Bhagavān Rādhā-Kṛṣṇa. It is a song sung in Saṁskṛta language and has eighteen chapters.  It proves:</p>
<h3 style="text-align: left;">1. ONE GOD: </h3>
<p style="text-align: left;"  class="indent">There are instances in the Puranas (part of Hinduism's set of scriptures), where God's physical form is described as Lord Shiva (See Shiv Puran), whereas at other times it is said that "one supreme entity divides itself into three forms 'Trimurti' - Creator (Lord Brahma), Sustainer (Lord Vishnu) and Destroyer (Lord Shiva), inorder to delegate Their functions" (see Vishnu Purana 1.2.66). To the respectful Hindu, this makes sense. However, to the questioning one, this may seem complicated. Here, the oath book clarifies the situation. 'One God' concept in 'Sanatana Dharma'  is explained when Arjuna sees "all the dieties/Gods" in the universal form of Śrī Śrī Bhagavān  Rādhā-Kṛṣṇa. See its Chapter 11 Verse 15. </p> 
<p style="text-align: left;"  class="indent"> &nbsp&nbsp&nbsp In relation to the synthesising Vishnu Purans 'Trimurti' concept back into the 'one supreme entity', Lord Śrī Śrī Bhagavān  Rādhā-Kṛṣṇa, the manifestation/Avatar of Śrī Vishnu (the sustainer) explicitly calls Himself [Herself/Theirself] 'the creator' in Chapter 4 verses 13 and 14, and 'the destroyer' in Chapter 11 Verse 32. Further, there are instances where many thousand dieties are mentioned in the scriptures such as Indra, the king of the Gods who attacks  Śrī Śrī Bhagavān  Rādhā-Kṛṣṇa in Śrīmad-Bhāgavatam text's Cantoh ten chapter 37. God Himself [Herself/ Theirself] clarifies the concept of such 'Gods' in Chapter 4 Verse 12 (Ramsukhdas, 2006, Pg. 493), i.e. they report to Him [/Her/Them].</p>
<h3 style="text-align: left;">2. CASTE SYSTEM: </h3>
<p style="text-align: left;"  class="indent">Natively, it is referred to as the VARŅA system and lacks the stigma that the phrase "CASTE SYSTEM" carries. </p>
<h3 style="text-align: left;">2.1 WHY IS THERE A VARŅA SYSTEM?</h3>
<p style="text-align: left;"  class="indent">Identifies that the Varṇa system is an economic 'division of labour' construct designed by Lord's arrangement to achieve 'economies of scale', in order to enable holistic progress of society. See Duties of the Four Varṇas in Chapter 18 Verses 41-44. </p>
<h3 style="text-align: left;">2.2 VARŅA SYSTEM IS NOT HERIDITARY:</h3>  
<p style="text-align: left;"  class="indent">What category an adherent belongs in the Varṇa System is based entirely on Guṇa (aptitude/ inner temperament) and Karma (actions). See Chapter 4 Verse 13.</p>
<h3 style="text-align: left;">2.3 THERE IS NO PRESCRIBED DISCRIMINATION IN VARŅA SYSTEM:</h3>
<p style="text-align: left;" class="indent">Spiritual eligibility is universal and God is equally available to all. In fact, the loving God  Śrī Śrī Rādhā-Kṛṣṇa goes to lengths to refute any possible chance of discrimination in the varņa system, arising from biological factors or the Bonafide roles humans play in society, in Chapter 9 Verse 32.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;"  class="indent">Hence, it is a way of life, which is practiced by over billion people across the world. It is also the oldest known faith, still being celebrated on Mother Earth:</p>
<p style="text-align: left;"  class="indent">- Śrīmad Bhagavad Gītā Jayanti celebrated on 01 December 2025 at <a href="https://www.svwt.org.nz/events-calendar-2023">Wainuiomata Temple</a> by <a href="https://www.chinmaya.org.nz/chinmaya-events/">Chinmaya Mission New Zealand</a>. It is the anniversary of the day as per lunar calendar, when Śrī Śrī Bhagavān  Rādhā-Kṛṣṇa first spoke the Bhagavad Gītā to Arjuna, for human welfare in 3067 B.C.E. The Gregorian Calendar date for this day that year being 22 November (Achar, 2014, Pg. 29). Please see above seven year old Laavya Sarna, daughter of Jay Sarna depicted propitiating Śrī Śrī Bhagavān  Rādhā-Kṛṣṇa on 'Georgian Calendar' equivalent five thousand and ninety second (5092) anniversary date, of this 'rescue of humanity' event in <a href="./misconceptions.php#mm1gitajayanti">ITEM #1</a>.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">𝘕𝘰𝘵𝘦: 𝘛𝘩𝘪𝘴 𝘱𝘰𝘴𝘵 𝘩𝘢𝘴 𝘢𝘭𝘴𝘰 𝘣𝘦𝘦𝘯 𝘵𝘳𝘢𝘯𝘴𝘭𝘢𝘵𝘦𝘥 𝘪𝘯𝘵𝘰 𝘏𝘪𝘯𝘥𝘶𝘴𝘵𝘢𝘯𝘪 𝘭𝘢𝘯𝘨𝘶𝘢𝘨𝘦 𝘣𝘦𝘭𝘰𝘸. 𝘍𝘰𝘳 𝘤𝘰𝘯𝘵𝘦𝘹𝘵 𝘰𝘯 𝘸𝘩𝘢𝘵 𝘵𝘩𝘦 Ś𝘳ī𝘮𝘢𝘥 𝘉𝘩𝘢𝘨𝘢𝘷𝘢𝘥 Gī𝘵ā 𝘵𝘦𝘹𝘵 is, 𝘱𝘭𝘦𝘢𝘴𝘦 𝘴𝘦𝘦 𝘈𝘱𝘱𝘦𝘯𝘥𝘪𝘹 1.0. 𝘍𝘪𝘯𝘢𝘭𝘭𝘺, 𝘵𝘰 𝘣𝘦 𝘩𝘰𝘯𝘦𝘴𝘵, 𝘵𝘩𝘦𝘳𝘦 𝘢𝘳𝘦 <a href="./misconception-root-cause.php">𝘨𝘦𝘯𝘶𝘪𝘯𝘦 𝘳𝘦𝘢𝘴𝘰𝘯𝘴</a> 𝘧𝘰𝘳 𝘵𝘩𝘦 𝘤𝘰𝘯𝘧𝘶𝘴𝘪𝘰𝘯𝘴 𝘱𝘦𝘰𝘱𝘭𝘦 𝘩𝘢𝘷𝘦 𝘳𝘦𝘭𝘢𝘵𝘪𝘯𝘨 𝘵𝘰 '𝘚𝘢𝘯𝘢𝘵𝘢𝘯𝘢 𝘋𝘩𝘢𝘳𝘮𝘢'.</p>
<br><br>My Respects to all
<br><br>Imparting of this knowledge is presented as my humble offering at the feet of  Śrī Śrī Bhagavān  Rādhā-Kṛṣṇa. 
<br><br><b>This is also "the One God"/"Lord Sita Ram" of my mentor 'Father of Modern India' Mahatma Gandhi ji (Ramsukhdas, 2006, Pg. 483).</b>
<br><br><h1 id="hindi">हिंदू धर्म / सनातन धर्म कि सच्चाई को स्पष्ट करना, मेरी समझ के अनुसार - श्रीमद् भगवद् गीता की 5092वीं वर्षगांठ का उत्सव</h1>
<br>----------------------
<p style="text-align: left;"  class="indent">मैं इस बात से बहुत परेशान हूँ कि अधिकांश लोग कहते हैं कि हिंदू धर्म के पास कोई शपथ-पुस्तक नहीं है, और कि हिंदू धर्म बहुदेववादी है / 'एक भगवान नहीं है'। यह मेरे दिल को बहुत क्रोध से भर देता है कि यहाँ तक कि कई हिंदू लोग भी इन झूठों को दोहराते हैं और इसे दृढ़ता से मानते हैं। मैं इसे एक गृहयुद्ध की तरह देखता हूँ।
लेकिन, क्योंकि मैं महात्मा गांधी जी का अहिंसक अनुयायी हूँ, इसलिए कृपया यहाँ 'सनातन धर्म' / हिंदू धर्म के शपथ-पुस्तक के प्रमाण देखें, जो 'सनातन धर्म' में 'एक भगवान' के विचार को सिद्ध करता है (प्रमाण के लिए, इसके अध्याय 11 श्लोक 15 को देखें): </p>
<p style="text-align: left;" class="indent">- श्रीमद्भगवद्गीता की वर्षगांठ/जयंती 01 दिसंबर 2025 को लोअर हट्ट (न्यूजीलैंड) के <a href="https://www.svwt.org.nz/events-calendar-2023">वाइनुइओमाटा मंदिर</a> में <a href="https://www.chinmaya.org.nz/chinmaya-events/">चिन्मय मिशन न्यूजीलैंड</a> द्वारा मनाई गई। यह चंद्र कैलेंडर आधारित पंचांग के अनुसार उस दिन की वर्षगांठ है, जब श्री भगवान राधा कृष्ण ने मानव कल्याण के लिए ईसा पूर्व 3067 में अर्जुन को भगवद् गीता का उपदेश दिया था। उस वर्ष ग्रेगोरियन पंचांग के अनुसार यह दिन 22 नवंबर को पड़ा था (आचार, 2014, पृष्ठ 29)। <b><a href="./misconceptions.php#mm1gitajayanti">ऊपर</a></b> ज्योतिर्मय सरना की बेटी, सात वर्षीय लाव्या सरना की एक तस्वीर है जिसमें वह इस पवित्र गीत की 'उत्पत्ति तिथि' की 5092वीं वर्षगांठ पर श्री श्री भगवान राधाकृष्ण को प्रार्थना कर रही हैं, उत्सव के दौरान।</p>
<p style="text-align: left;"  class="indent">इस ज्ञान को देने को मैं भगवान के चरणों में अपनी नम्र भेंट के रूप में प्रस्तुत करता हूँ। 
<B><p style="text-align: center;">यही आधुनिक भारत के पिता और हमारे बड़े महात्मा गांधी जी के "भगवान सीता राम" भी हैं (रामसुखदास, १९९७, पृष्ठ.२२६)</p></B>
<br><br>नोट: श्रीमद्भगवद्गीता पाठ के संदर्भ के लिए कृपया Appendix 1.0/परिशिष्ट 1.0 देखें। अंत में, ईमानदारी से कहूँ तो, सनातन धर्म को लेकर लोगों में जो भ्रम हैं, उनके <a href="./misconception-root-cause.php">कुछ वास्तविक कारण हैं</a>, जैसा कि यहाँ बताया गया है। लेकिन मैंने यहाँ उन पर चर्चा नहीं की है, क्योंकि उनका खंडन करना सामान्य बातचीत के दायरे से बाहर है, क्योंकि उनमें गहन बहस और तथ्य-जाँच की आवश्यकता होती है।
<br><br>सभी को सम्मान</p>
